message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "jmjax: Joint Models for Longitudinal and Survival Data via JAX"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guo
    given-names: Changbin
    email: jmjaxmaintainer@gmail.com
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-25
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22950084
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jmjaxmaintainer-jpg/jmjax"
abstract: >-
  Shared-parameter joint models for longitudinal and time-to-event data,
  fitted in R with a JAX/NumPyro backend: maximum likelihood with adaptive
  Gauss-Hermite quadrature, and Bayesian estimation with the No-U-Turn
  sampler.
keywords:
  - joint models
  - survival analysis
  - longitudinal data
  - Hamiltonian Monte Carlo
  - R
